    thinking: "**Reviewing Design Constraints**\n\nI\'m now diving into the design guidelines, specifically focusing on the instructions provided in `design-guidelines`. I\'m starting by carefully reviewing the points on avoiding generic AI defaults, which seem straightforward. After that, I\'ll select a theme.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Style**\n\nI\'ve decided on a \"luxury dark\" aesthetic with a dark theme as a starting point, integrating glowing accents and tactile-feeling controls. I\'ve chosen a deep space/carbon black color palette for the background. I\'m focusing on vivid accents, too: Electric Cyan/Sonic Blue for Deck A, Electric Amber/Warm Gold for Deck B, Pulse Violet/Magenta for DSP, and Matrix Emerald for live signals. These colors will emphasize animated meters, and other interactive elements. I\'m imagining crisp typography and some fun animated elements. Now, I\'m defining the data layer with Room Database, starting with the `TrackEntity`.\n\n\n**Outlining Data Structure**\n\nI\'m currently formalizing the data schema. I\'ve defined entities for `Track`, `Playlist`, `PlaylistTrackCrossRef`, `DspPreset`, and `AuraDeckDao` within the `RoomDatabase`, including pre-population of demo tracks and presets. I\'m focusing on the relationship between playlists and tracks.\n\n\n**Implementing Audio Effects**\n\nI\'m now integrating audio effects into the playback engine. I\'m focusing on `Equalizer`, `BassBoost`, and `Virtualizer`, implementing fallbacks for unsupported hardware. I\'m leveraging `DynamicsProcessing` for API 28+, ensuring robust performance across different devices. My focus is on a smooth user experience, even with varied hardware capabilities.\n\n\n\n**Integrating Audio Stream Sources**\n\nI\'m now integrating stream sources, specifically focusing on `StreamResolver.kt`. This includes parsing YouTube URLs, resolving direct audio streams from various sources (YouTube, HTTP/HTTPS, and local files). It\'s also going to handle `ACTION_SEND` intents to accept shared links seamlessly. Now I am working on the audio visualization pipeline.\n\n**Designing Audio Visualizations**\n\nCurrently, I\'m working on the `VisualizerEngine.kt` and the Composable part. I\'ve got four distinct modes: Neon Spectrum, a circular waveform, and a Lissajous display. I\'m focusing on real-time capture of the audio waveform and FFT frequency spectrum, aiming for dynamic and engaging visuals. I\'m prioritizing responsiveness and smoothness.\n\n\n**Developing UI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now implementing new visual elements. I\'m focusing on dynamic, floating, reactive particles responding to sound transients, alongside animated Lissajous curves. I\'m also ensuring smooth visuals in test environments by generating simulated FFT data. I am working on the foreground playback service with media notifications, artwork, and controls for a seamless user experience. Next, I am working on the top bar and deck views.\n\n\n**Constructing User Interface**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user interface elements. I\'m focusing on Deck B\'s animations \342\200\223 a realistic vinyl platter with scratch effects, track details, and controls. The center mixer includes dual VU meters, a crossfader, and master volume. I\'m also planning the main views for the mixer, audio effects, and visualizer.\n\n\n**Refining App Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating playlists, including curated options and a stream library with a search bar and custom URL input. I\'m building a reactive, fullscreen visualizer with mode switching and color themes. I\'m also ensuring the test files for the project are checked and appropriately updated to test the new components. Finally, I\'m reviewing and updating the manifest with relevant permissions, the AuraPlaybackService and intent filters for ACTION_SEND and ACTION_VIEW on MainActivity.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 247869644
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
