  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the Compose UI components now. Specifically, I\'m thinking about the visual elements of AuraDeck that will evoke a high-end audiophile console feel. Right now, I\'m focused on the `VisualizerSurface.kt` component, particularly its canvas rendering and four distinct modes. The first mode I\'m planning out is the `NEON_SPECTRUM`. This one will focus on neon gradient bars, glow effects, and peak caps.\n\n\n**Refining Visualizer Modes**\n\nI\'ve been iterating on the visualizer modes: `NEON_SPECTRUM` is taking shape with gravity falloff and dual-hue options, like cyan/amber or violet. The `CIRCULAR_WAVE` mode\'s now envisioned as a radial oscilloscope with a bass-pulsing center glow, while `LISSAJOUS_PHASE` is a polar goniometer with a cool phosphor trail. Finally, `LIQUID_PARTICLES` will be a fluid particle cluster responding to audio.\n\n\n**Expanding UI Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed audio responsiveness metrics into the fullscreen visualizer within `VisualizerStudioScreen.kt`. It\'ll have chips for mode selection alongside a live FFT 64-band readout. The LibraryScreen\'s getting a YouTube stream ingest card with a Deck selector and hi-res audio badges for tracks. I\'m also planning the `ui/components/VisualizerSurface` component.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 201873879
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
