  planner_response {
    response: "I have built **AuraDeck**, an audiophile dual-deck media player application with a high-fidelity dark console aesthetic.\n\n### Functional and Visual Overview\n\n- **Dual-Deck DJ Console**:\n  - **Turntable Platters**: Features realistic vinyl grooved platters with rotating physics synchronized to playback speed, live album artwork spindles, and touch drag scrubbing for vinyl scratching.\n  - **Deck A & B Independence**: Dedicated transport controls for each deck, including CUE points, automatic BPM counter and synchronization, pitch adjustment faders (0.5x to 2.0x), and seamless looping.\n  - **Hardware Crossfader & Mixer**: Smooth constant-power crossfader with instant cut switches (`CUT A` / `CUT B`) and dual-channel segmented LED VU meters with peak level warning indicators.\n\n- **Audiophile DSP Suite**:\n  - **10-Band Graphic Equalizer**: Precision vertical tactile faders ranging from 31Hz to 16kHz with \302\26112 dB gain controls and center zero detents.\n  - **Acoustic Enhancement Engines**: Rotary dials controlling 3D HRTF headset surround spatialization and harmonic bass exciter strength.\n  - **Dynamics Processing**: Integrated multiband compressor and peak limiter to normalize dynamics and eliminate digital clipping distortion.\n  - **Soundstage Presets**: One-tap profiles including Audiophile Clarity, Deep Bass, 3D Holographic, Club & Electronic, Vocal Intimacy, and Acoustic.\n\n- **Real-Time Visualizer Studio**:\n  - **4 Dynamic Modes**: Switchable between Neon Multi-Bar Spectrum (with gravity-decay peak falloff), 360\302\260 Radial Waveform Oscilloscope, Stereo Goniometer (Lissajous phase correlation), and Liquid Particle fields.\n  - **Live Acoustic Telemetry**: Sub-bass, midrange, and treble frequency energy bars rendering at 60 FPS.\n\n- **Library & Stream Ingestion**:\n  - **YouTube & Web Audio Ingestion**: Input stream resolver capable of resolving YouTube links, shorts, and direct web audio streams directly into Deck A or Deck B.\n  - **Local Device Storage**: Zero-permission document picker integration for importing local lossless audio files.\n  - **Background Playback**: Foreground service integration with system media notification and partial wake lock for uninterrupted screen-off listening."
    modified_response: "I have built **AuraDeck**, an audiophile dual-deck media player application with a high-fidelity dark console aesthetic.\n\n### Functional and Visual Overview\n\n- **Dual-Deck DJ Console**:\n  - **Turntable Platters**: Features realistic vinyl grooved platters with rotating physics synchronized to playback speed, live album artwork spindles, and touch drag scrubbing for vinyl scratching.\n  - **Deck A & B Independence**: Dedicated transport controls for each deck, including CUE points, automatic BPM counter and synchronization, pitch adjustment faders (0.5x to 2.0x), and seamless looping.\n  - **Hardware Crossfader & Mixer**: Smooth constant-power crossfader with instant cut switches (`CUT A` / `CUT B`) and dual-channel segmented LED VU meters with peak level warning indicators.\n\n- **Audiophile DSP Suite**:\n  - **10-Band Graphic Equalizer**: Precision vertical tactile faders ranging from 31Hz to 16kHz with \302\26112 dB gain controls and center zero detents.\n  - **Acoustic Enhancement Engines**: Rotary dials controlling 3D HRTF headset surround spatialization and harmonic bass exciter strength.\n  - **Dynamics Processing**: Integrated multiband compressor and peak limiter to normalize dynamics and eliminate digital clipping distortion.\n  - **Soundstage Presets**: One-tap profiles including Audiophile Clarity, Deep Bass, 3D Holographic, Club & Electronic, Vocal Intimacy, and Acoustic.\n\n- **Real-Time Visualizer Studio**:\n  - **4 Dynamic Modes**: Switchable between Neon Multi-Bar Spectrum (with gravity-decay peak falloff), 360\302\260 Radial Waveform Oscilloscope, Stereo Goniometer (Lissajous phase correlation), and Liquid Particle fields.\n  - **Live Acoustic Telemetry**: Sub-bass, midrange, and treble frequency energy bars rendering at 60 FPS.\n\n- **Library & Stream Ingestion**:\n  - **YouTube & Web Audio Ingestion**: Input stream resolver capable of resolving YouTube links, shorts, and direct web audio streams directly into Deck A or Deck B.\n  - **Local Device Storage**: Zero-permission document picker integration for importing local lossless audio files.\n  - **Background Playback**: Foreground service integration with system media notification and partial wake lock for uninterrupted screen-off listening."
