  search_web {
    query: "youtubei/v1/player android client request payload streamingData audio"
    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGaiYi7Lv4lJz0j_8fh--k_97OdBsT7Gl0Rz2cccQ3vKpufcHDC2D-ncd9ooQLDrlUf2_fMN2GM4Q-ioxlGEM6sxAkAgDDLCxeqm7LL2rI8JaLmUeW_10fVSykdmVMOHm8NkJv2Q18RVp3Hydt_lsgMzjrZYU7HZg=="
      title: "tyrrrz.me"
    }
    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQExUVtrpjV_UhTAOXPuqhmFLJguNkyHP9EcVCv-0Pr2fzY_vyHH7dPkFQdC9xq2CTr3j-4NuFPoCcd_xpC3QNYcxNTZGHU47Cs2P-v8iXRCUsI5yiQzLuj4axRhIPTz3V_u13FxGCmHrRg0RHhXWExdbol_Aj1aoYoVxC1dQR0="
      title: "github.com"
    }
    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFeIzHoYoqZmaMdw5JtNegXIwx5dleRfRuQcgX9QYGOHg1vt8FHnLPCqPFRkyTWs2z7zjbKMJ7kCR6q3ZMXNXTFyPYUuG3d4EXWb4KxhfuaF137yXNKzyoRlCAktwz_9WTUnQ10tsvkRpgoWL4f6Zpdm5TSWE2-cRGkXCDo6ys9q_cocm-dUJ9rF-Nzb8-dBQvmHjTpHczIPVgwH_NeE1y9SsEelOcGSfM="
      title: "stackoverflow.com"
    }
    summary: "The `youtubei/v1/player` endpoint, when accessed by an Android client, primarily receives a request payload containing a `videoId` and a `context` object with client-specific information (e.g., `clientName`, `clientVersion`, `hl` for language, `gl` for location, `visitorData`). The request payload itself does not typically include a `streamingData.audio` field.[1][2][3]\n\nInstead, the `streamingData` object is part of the *response* returned by the `youtubei/v1/player` endpoint. This response provides the necessary information for the player to stream the video and audio. If a video is playable, the `streamingData` object will contain a list of available streams.[1]\n\nWithin the `streamingData` object in the API response, audio stream information is typically found within two arrays:\n*   **`formats`**: This array may contain pre-combined video and audio streams.[2]\n*   **`adaptiveFormats`**: This is described as the \"modern way\" and usually separates video and audio streams, offering more flexibility.[2]\n\nEach entry within these `formats` or `adaptiveFormats` arrays is a stream descriptor that includes a temporary, signed `url` pointing to Google\'s video delivery servers, from which the actual media (including audio) can be streamed.[2]\n\nSources:\n[1] [tyrrrz.me](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGaiYi7Lv4lJz0j_8fh--k_97OdBsT7Gl0Rz2cccQ3vKpufcHDC2D-ncd9ooQLDrlUf2_fMN2GM4Q-ioxlGEM6sxAkAgDDLCxeqm7LL2rI8JaLmUeW_10fVSykdmVMOHm8NkJv2Q18RVp3Hydt_lsgMzjrZYU7HZg==)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQExUVtrpjV_UhTAOXPuqhmFLJguNkyHP9EcVCv-0Pr2fzY_vyHH7dPkFQdC9xq2CTr3j-4NuFPoCcd_xpC3QNYcxNTZGHU47Cs2P-v8iXRCUsI5yiQzLuj4axRhIPTz3V_u13FxGCmHrRg0RHhXWExdbol_Aj1aoYoVxC1dQR0=)\n[3] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFeIzHoYoqZmaMdw5JtNegXIwx5dleRfRuQcgX9QYGOHg1vt8FHnLPCqPFRkyTWs2z7zjbKMJ7kCR6q3ZMXNXTFyPYUuG3d4EXWb4KxhfuaF137yXNKzyoRlCAktwz_9WTUnQ10tsvkRpgoWL4f6Zpdm5TSWE2-cRGkXCDo6ys9q_cocm-dUJ9rF-Nzb8-dBQvmHjTpHczIPVgwH_NeE1y9SsEelOcGSfM=)"
