  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Visualizer Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `VisualizerEngine.kt` file. I\'m exploring the logic that simulates soundwaves when a visualizer isn\'t present or is disabled. It\'s an interesting implementation, and I\'m diving deeper into how it achieves that responsive organic effect.\n\n\n**Analyzing Visualizer Issues**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a key issue: the `generateSyntheticFrame` function was running continuously at 60Hz, regardless of playback state. This explains the visualizer\'s persistent activity, even when music is paused. Furthermore, I\'ve identified the root cause of the hardware visualizer\'s malfunction. It\'s the missing `android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO` permission, which was never requested at runtime.\n\n\n**Fixing Audio Permission Errors**\n\nI\'ve determined the core problem: a `SecurityException` due to missing `RECORD_AUDIO` permission. The app was failing to attach the hardware visualizer. To remedy this, I\'m integrating permission requests within `MainActivity`. I\'m also ensuring the `VisualizerEngine` receives playback state updates: `isPlaying`, `bpm`, `vuLevel`, and `positionMs`, which is critical for accurate visual representation. I am now updating the logic to correctly decay visualizer values when audio is paused.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 278787237
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
