  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Embedding Alternatives**\n\nI\'m now exploring alternatives to direct Invidious instances. Rate limiting and redirection are proving troublesome. I\'m pivoting towards leveraging YouTube\'s embed feature, specifically the HTML `<iframe>` method, to see if it provides a more stable solution for incorporating video content.\n\n\n**Evaluating WebView Integration**\n\nI\'ve been examining the potential of integrating an Android `WebView` that leverages the official YouTube IFrame Player. This approach circumvents common issues like 403 errors and signature problems, as it\'s directly from Google. This offers granular control through the JavaScript API, including playback state, buffering information, and time updates. It provides direct device-level audio output, eliminating external proxy dependencies, offering a powerful solution for various YouTube content including shorts and music.\n\n\n**Implementing YouTube Bridge**\n\nI\'ve successfully implemented a YouTube player bridge, fetching metadata immediately and setting up the player for either Deck A or Deck B. I\'ve integrated a buffering bar to give a clear status update: \"CONNECTING TO YOUTUBE STREAM...\" transitioning to \"BUFFERING...\" then automatic playback. Core controls like play, pause, seek, and volume are all functional, alongside crossfader and scratch functionality. The crucial component that works is the visualizer, leveraging `RECORD_AUDIO` permission to synchronize with system audio for both local and YouTube streams using Visualizer(0), which includes BPM and VU meter.\n\n\n**Enhancing Media Control**\n\nI\'m now integrating a comprehensive media control system. This includes a `MediaStyle` notification with standard controls, lock screen media card support, and a request for `POST_NOTIFICATIONS` permission. I\'m also adding functionality to remove local songs directly from the `LibraryScreen` via a delete button, which updates the Room database and the UI. This is a crucial addition to improve local track management.\n\n\n\n**Refining Player Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on fine-tuning the YouTube integration. The phase calculation, modulated by VU levels and beat pulses, is working. I\'ve refined the logic to automatically add and play tracks from shared URLs, be they YouTube or audio links, and loading directly to the active deck. I\'m adding a prominent buffering indicator with a progress bar and status chip, e.g., \"BUFFERING YOUTUBE STREAM...\" to confirm streams are loading. I\'ve corrected the error with YouTube links not playing. Raw links were given to the wrong player!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 163327367
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
