  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Integrating YouTube Bridge**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on integrating the `YouTubeAudioBridge` into `DualDeckAudioEngine.kt`. I\'ve started by adding two nullable `YouTubeAudioBridge` instances, `ytPlayerA` and `ytPlayerB`. My next step is to see how this affects `DeckUiState`.\n\n\n**Refining YouTube Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how YouTube tracks are loaded and managed. I\'m checking if the track URI starts with \"youtube:\" or \"yt:\", or if it\'s a valid YouTube URL. If it\'s a YouTube track, I pause or reset the respective MediaPlayer and extract the video ID. Then, I update the `DeckUiState`, setting `isLoading`, `isBuffering`, `bufferPercent`, and `statusText` accordingly, as well as setting `isYoutubeTrack` to true.\n\n\n**Managing Audio Transitions**\n\nI\'ve been working on managing the transitions between YouTube and other audio sources. Now, when a YouTube track is selected, the correct `ytPlayer` loads the video and updates the UI accordingly, after checking for the right URI format. In other audio sources, the YouTube player is stopped or paused, and the local MediaPlayer takes over. I\'ve also added handling for pausing and playing YouTube tracks using `togglePlayPause`.\n\n\n**Refining Player Interaction**\n\nI\'m now implementing logic to seamlessly integrate YouTube tracks into existing controls. I\'ve ensured YouTube tracks can properly seek to specific points and adjust playback speed using `seekTo` and `setDeckSpeed`.  I\'ve also refined the volume adjustments, as both MediaPlayer and YouTube player now react smoothly to crossfader and master volume changes, which I\'ve checked with `recalculateVolumes()`.  Finally, I\'m integrating VU meter calculations for YouTube tracks in `updatePlaybackPositionsAndVu()`.\n\n\n**Calculating VU Levels**\n\nI\'m now focusing on calculating the VU meter levels accurately for both decks. I\'m introducing a slight audio jitter to make the meters feel more natural, incorporating this with a base level that accounts for volume, crossfader, and master volume. I\'m ensuring the VU level falls off to 0 when neither player is active on a deck. Additionally, I\'ve implemented a new `unloadDeck` function in `DualDeckAudioEngine` to stop and reset the players, including the YouTube players, upon unloading a deck. My next task is to assess how `VisualizerEngine` should be updated based on player state.\n\n\n**Implementing Visualizer Decay**\n\nI\'m now implementing `decayToSilence`, gradually reducing the visualizer values for a smoother, more natural falloff when audio isn\'t active. I\'m focusing on the `fftMagnitudes`, `peakMagnitudes`, and `waveformPoints` components of the `VisualizerFrame`, with energy levels for bass, mid and high ranges. I\'m also implementing beat synchronization, adding a beat-synchronized frame by calculating the beat interval and applying an exponential decay to the current VU level.\n\n\n**Visualizing Audio Dynamics**\n\nI\'m now refining the visualizer\'s response to audio input. I\'ve focused on syncing the visualizer\'s energy levels with the music\'s dynamics, ensuring the bass frequencies pulse with the beat. The waveform now accurately vibrates based on the song\'s energy and amplitude, and the mid and high energies mirror the VU meter and harmonic rhythm. When the audio is paused, the visualizer immediately stops with `decayToSilence()`. I\'m now exploring `AuraDeckViewModel.kt` to understand how the visualizer\'s state is updated based on playback.\n\n\n**Integrating Media Session**\n\nI\'m now integrating `MediaSessionCompat` into `AuraPlaybackService.kt` to enhance the lock screen and notification experience. I\'ve initiated the `MediaSessionCompat` and set up the callback for play and pause actions. I need to make the audio engine toggle the correct deck when the user triggers these actions from the notification or lock screen. I\'m focusing on ensuring seamless integration with the existing `togglePlayPause` logic and am considering how to handle track changes.\n\n\n**Implementing Media Session Controls**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating media session controls. I\'ve implemented `MediaSessionCompat.Callback` to handle `skipNext`, `skipPrevious`, `seekTo`, and `stop` actions, and linked them to the audio engine\'s corresponding functions. I\'ve updated the `PlaybackStateCompat` to reflect the playback state and supported actions. I\'m updating the `MediaMetadataCompat` to reflect the current track details, title and artist.\n\n\n**Constructing Notification Details**\n\nI\'m now building out the media notification, starting with setting the album title to \"AuraDeck Audiophile\" in the metadata, including duration. I\'m building pending intents for previous, play/pause, next, and stop actions. I\'m also using `MediaStyle` for the notification and adding actions for the controls. The notification will be visible on the lock screen.\n\n\n**Refining Track Resolution**\n\nI\'m now diving into `StreamResolver.kt` to enhance how YouTube URLs are handled. I\'ve updated the regex for YouTube URLs to be more robust, ensuring that even complex links are correctly parsed. Next, I\'m integrating metadata fetching from the YouTube oEmbed endpoint to retrieve track information, including title, author, thumbnail, and duration. Finally, I\'ll update the `ResolvedTrackInfo` with the new information and handle BPM where possible. I\'m focusing on ensuring it works robustly in the **swipe-down notification drawer**!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 879152238
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
