  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed all the requested fixes and features:\n\n- **Lock Screen & Notification Drawer Media Controls**:\n  - Configured `MediaSessionCompat` and `MediaNotificationCompat.MediaStyle` in the foreground playback service.\n  - Linked bidirectional media playback callbacks (`onPlay`, `onPause`, `onSkipToNext`, `onSkipToPrevious`, `onSeekTo`) to the active DJ deck.\n  - Provided prominent actions for Previous, Play/Pause, Next, and Stop with `VISIBILITY_PUBLIC` so playback can be controlled directly from the lock screen and notification pull-down.\n\n- **Remove Songs from Library**:\n  - Added a dedicated delete button on each track entry in the Library view.\n  - Deleting a track removes it from the local database and safely unloads it from Deck A or Deck B if active.\n\n- **Beat-Synchronized Visualizer**:\n  - Linked real-time playback telemetry (BPM, position, VU amplitude, playing status) directly to the visualizer render engine.\n  - When playback is paused or stopped, the visualizer decays to silence immediately rather than running indefinitely.\n  - When playing, the visuals pulse rhythmically in sync with the beat.\n\n- **YouTube Loading & Buffering Status**:\n  - Added dedicated progress bars and buffering text readouts to both deck cards and the stream ingestion card.\n  - Clearly displays real-time loading feedback while YouTube streams and metadata are being resolved and buffered.\n\n- **Reliable YouTube Playback & Auto-Play on Share**:\n  - Integrated `YouTubeAudioBridge` to stream and manage YouTube audio sources.\n  - Updated the application\'s share target handler so that sharing any audio link or YouTube URL immediately adds the track to the library, assigns it to Deck A, and begins playback automatically."
    modified_response: "I have completed all the requested fixes and features:\n\n- **Lock Screen & Notification Drawer Media Controls**:\n  - Configured `MediaSessionCompat` and `MediaNotificationCompat.MediaStyle` in the foreground playback service.\n  - Linked bidirectional media playback callbacks (`onPlay`, `onPause`, `onSkipToNext`, `onSkipToPrevious`, `onSeekTo`) to the active DJ deck.\n  - Provided prominent actions for Previous, Play/Pause, Next, and Stop with `VISIBILITY_PUBLIC` so playback can be controlled directly from the lock screen and notification pull-down.\n\n- **Remove Songs from Library**:\n  - Added a dedicated delete button on each track entry in the Library view.\n  - Deleting a track removes it from the local database and safely unloads it from Deck A or Deck B if active.\n\n- **Beat-Synchronized Visualizer**:\n  - Linked real-time playback telemetry (BPM, position, VU amplitude, playing status) directly to the visualizer render engine.\n  - When playback is paused or stopped, the visualizer decays to silence immediately rather than running indefinitely.\n  - When playing, the visuals pulse rhythmically in sync with the beat.\n\n- **YouTube Loading & Buffering Status**:\n  - Added dedicated progress bars and buffering text readouts to both deck cards and the stream ingestion card.\n  - Clearly displays real-time loading feedback while YouTube streams and metadata are being resolved and buffered.\n\n- **Reliable YouTube Playback & Auto-Play on Share**:\n  - Integrated `YouTubeAudioBridge` to stream and manage YouTube audio sources.\n  - Updated the application\'s share target handler so that sharing any audio link or YouTube URL immediately adds the track to the library, assigns it to Deck A, and begins playback automatically."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
