  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering UI Configurations**\n\nI\'ve been focusing on the UI\'s adaptability based on deck selection. The ability to switch between one and two deck modes is the current priority. The default will be one deck mode, which includes a large play area.\n\n\n**Investigating Audio Output**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the audio output issues. I need to understand why no sound is being produced. Specifically, I\'m scrutinizing `DualDeckAudioEngine.kt` and `AudioEngineDsp.kt`, alongside volume controls and crossfader implementation. The crossfader\'s impact in single-deck mode is a key area of concern, as is ensuring correct volume levels. I\'m focusing on ensuring audio streams are output correctly.\n\n\n**Analyzing Audio Initialization**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the YouTube audio issue. It seems a headless WebView, like the one in `YouTubeAudioBridge.kt`, might be the problem. The audio might be throttled or muted if it\'s not attached to a visible view hierarchy. I\'m also retracing the audio initialization in `loadTrack` to ensure recalculation and start happen in the right order. I\'m focusing on ensuring audio streams are output correctly, and crossfader\'s bypass behavior. The default and initial tracks are also relevant, so I\'m investigating how these are loaded to further address the problem.\n\n\n**Addressing WebView Restrictions**\n\nI\'ve realized that the headless WebView, as currently implemented, likely won\'t play audio due to Android\'s media playback restrictions and potentially muted `WebSettings`. Setting `mediaPlaybackRequiresUserGesture = false` is critical. Also, an unattached WebView pauses or fails to initialize audio. I\'m considering attaching a hidden `AndroidView` with the WebView to ensure proper initialization and playback. I\'m focusing on the YouTube Iframe player behavior in `YouTubeAudioBridge.kt`.\n\n\n**Confirming YouTube Iframe Playback**\n\nI\'ve realized that ensuring YouTube Iframe player audio requires explicit unmuting and setting the volume, even with `autoplay: 1`. I\'m now verifying if `player.unMute()` and `player.setVolume(100)` are called within `onPlayerReady`. Furthermore, attaching the WebView in Compose via `AndroidView` is critical for proper initialization and preventing audio throttling on Android. I\'m scrutinizing `Bridge.kt` for this.\n\n\n**Verifying Lifecycle Events**\n\nI\'m now investigating potential lifecycle issues. I need to confirm if `webView.onResume()` is ever called, and it wasn\'t! Offscreen WebViews are paused by default; timers and media playback are affected. This explains the audio issues. I\'ll need to confirm lifecycle management in `YouTubeAudioBridge.kt` and ensure the `webView` instance is properly resumed.\n\n**Examining Playback Timeline**\n\nI\'m now looking into the playback timeline\'s misbehavior. I\'m checking `DualDecksScreen.kt` and `DualDeckAudioEngine.kt`. Specifically, I\'m examining how `updatePlaybackPositionsAndVu` updates the current position and duration. Then I\'ll check how the timeline slider/seek bar is displayed and manipulated in `DualDecksScreen.kt`.\n\n**Evaluating Library UI Appearance**\n\nI\'m now examining the library UI, specifically `LibraryScreen.kt`, as I need to address reported visual irregularities. I\'m focusing on layout issues and visual consistency, per user feedback. I\'ll need to revise and enhance the user experience and interface of the library view.\n\n\n"
