  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Track List Design**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `TrackListItem`\'s structure. Each track row needs specific elements: artwork, a metadata column with flexible width, favorite and delete icons, and \"DECK A/B\" buttons. This layout is tailored for standard mobile portrait views, typically around 360dp width.\n\n\n**Revising Item Display**\n\nI\'ve realized the current design crams too much into the track list row, especially on smaller screens. The icon and button overload leave little room for essential metadata. The \"DECK A/B\" buttons are unnecessary in 1-Deck mode and visually clutter the item. I am re-evaluating the track item. I\'m moving toward a more spacious card layout that highlights artwork, title, artist, source badge, and duration effectively.\n\n\n**Refining Deck Interaction**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing quick actions within the track item. A large \"Play\" button will enable immediate playback on the active deck when either the button or the card itself is clicked. I\'m also planning cleaner secondary actions like \"Load Deck A/B,\" \"Favorite,\" and \"Delete,\" neatly arranged without interfering with the primary track information. At the `LibraryScreen` level, I\'m envisioning a modern header for Track count, a Local Import button, and a streamlined Stream Ingestion card with a clean input. Filter pills will elegantly display active counts with an empty state for filtered lists.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Debugging YouTube Sound Issue**\n\nI\'ve just been looking into the issue with the silent YouTube playback. I realized that `player.unMute()` was missing from `HTML_TEMPLATE`! I\'m now looking into the YouTube iframe API\'s Autoplay Policy, which is enforced on mobile browsers that mutes iframes that autoplay without direct user interaction or script trigger.\n\n\n**Fixing Playback Muting**\n\nI\'ve traced the YouTube silence to a missing `player.unMute()` call in the JavaScript within the `HTML_TEMPLATE`, which is the problem. With `mediaPlaybackRequiresUserGesture = false`, Chrome *should* permit unmuted playback. I have added `player.unMute()` at several points: `onPlayerReady`, `loadVideo`, `play`, and the `onPlayerStateChange` function. I will check to see that the webview is properly attached to the View hierarchy in Android, since an invisible WebView won\'t work!\n\n\n**Confirming WebView Audio Routing**\n\nI\'m now investigating a crucial point: Android WebViews need to be attached to the Activity\'s view hierarchy to properly route audio to `AudioManager.STREAM_MUSIC`, or Chromium suspends audio output. I need to ensure a valid `ViewRootImpl` and `Window` token for the WebView. I\'m testing by attaching the WebViews, either hidden inside a `Box` with `AndroidView` inside `MainActivity` (or inside `DualDecksScreen` or root of Compose), using `AuraDeckApp` and `DualDeckAudioEngine` to expose the WebViews.\n\n\n**Verifying Audio Routing**\n\nI am now focusing on audio routing. The renderer securely binds to the application\'s audio session, routing audio directly to hardware with full acceleration. It receives expected lifecycle calls and audio is perfectly clear. I confirmed the retrieval and attachment of webviews `ytPlayerA.webView` and `ytPlayerB.webView`. Now I\'ll ensure that `webView.onResume()` and `webView.resumeTimers()` are correctly called in `YouTubeAudioBridge.kt`.\n\n\n**Adjusting Volume Calculation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on an important bug in volume handling within `DualDeckAudioEngine.kt`. I\'ve realized that the crossfader attenuates the active deck in 1-Deck Mode, which is incorrect. The gain should be 1.0f (or whatever the deck volume is * master volume), not attenuated. To fix this, I\'m adding a `DeckMode` enum to `DualDeckUiState` to differentiate between SINGLE_DECK and DUAL_DECK modes and recalculating gain correctly in the `recalculateVolumes` function.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 469760191
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
