  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Screen Layout**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the user interface for the DualDecksScreen. The plan includes a mode switch at the top, allowing easy toggling between single-deck and dual-deck modes. The initial code sketch uses a Row with `SpaceBetween` arrangement for the mode selector.\n\n\n**Refining Deck Mode Switching**\n\nI\'ve refined the `FilterChip` implementation for deck mode selection. I\'m focusing on visual clarity, and readability of the button. The switch is currently rendered in the UI with a `Surface` shape and border, and the individual chip has a set of state colors. I am testing the code implementation, and its related `ViewModel`.\n\n\n**Developing Single Deck Display**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the single-deck display. I\'m focusing on the visual elements. I have plans for a segmented pill to toggle between decks A and B, when both are loaded. A large, rotating turntable platter with vinyl textures, album art, and reactive VU glow are also included. There\'s also a sleek metadata card.\n\n\n**Designing Deck Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed features for the single and dual decks. I\'m prioritizing a smooth DeckTimelineScrubber for both, crucial for responsiveness. Single-deck elements include a platter, metadata, and transport controls. The dual-deck mode incorporates a DJ mixer with crossfader, master controls, and side-by-side deck views. I\'m also looking at integrating the LibraryScreen.\n\n\n**Implementing Import Features**\n\nI\'m now designing the user interface for importing audio. I\'m prioritizing a prominent \"Import Local Audio\" button, complete with a folder icon and a clear track count badge. I\'ve also designed a segmented filter bar featuring options like \"ALL\", \"LOCAL\", and \"FAVORITES,\" each with associated counts.\n\nI\'m now developing the track card UI to enhance clarity. I\'ve opted for a rich slate-dark container with rounded corners. The design includes artwork, title, artist, and various badges displaying information like BPM and source. I\'ve added a large play button on the right for immediate song loading.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 24
      nanos: 168506267
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
