    thinking: "**Defining Track Layout**\n\nI\'ve been sketching out the `TrackListItem` layout. It\'s envisioned as a horizontal `Row`, with the artwork taking 48dp, followed by a 10dp spacer. Metadata will be weighted to fill remaining space. Then, the layout incorporates favorite and delete buttons (32dp each), plus Deck A and Deck B buttons (60dp each), and the remaining space of the `Row`.\n\n\n**Refining Track Item Layout**\n\nI\'ve hit a wall with the initial `TrackListItem` design. The fixed widths were way too rigid. The text was getting crushed, and buttons overflowed! I\'m now completely rethinking the layout, aiming for a 2-tier card structure that\'s both spacious and balanced. The top tier features a prominent artwork, spacious metadata, and a play button. The bottom tier houses action buttons and song details.\n\n\n"
