  planner_response {
    response: "All requested features, fixes, and design enhancements have been implemented and verified:\n\n- **Deck Mode Switching (1-Deck Default & 2-Decks Pro DJ Mode)**:\n  - Added a configuration toggle at the top of the Decks screen between **1 DECK (Solo)** and **2 DECKS (DJ)**, defaulting to 1-Deck mode.\n  - In **1-Deck Mode**, a dedicated solo audiophile console is presented featuring a large vinyl platter, expansive track metadata, audiophile spec tags (BPM, Key, Bit-Depth), smooth transport controls, and an interactive Channel A / Channel B selector.\n  - In **2-Decks Mode**, dual decks are displayed side-by-side with the center crossfader console, master rotary dial, and dual channel VU meters.\n\n- **Full Application Exit & Service Termination**:\n  - Added a dedicated **Power / Exit** action button in the top navigation bar.\n  - Tapping this opens a confirmation dialog that halts all deck playback, releases native `MediaPlayer` instances, stops the foreground `AuraPlaybackService`, clears notification controls, finishes active activities, and terminates the background process.\n\n- **Audio Playback & YouTube Sound Routing**:\n  - Resolved the YouTube silence issue by embedding the audio bridge WebViews directly into the active Compose hierarchy, forcing initialization unmuting and setting volume to 100% upon player readiness.\n  - Configured hardware audio session routing so audio plays through device speakers, headphones, or external DACs.\n\n- **Redesigned Library UI**:\n  - Fixed cramped track list items by transitioning to a clean 2-tier card layout. Song title and artist now receive full horizontal width with dedicated badges for source (**YouTube**, **Stream**, or **Local**), BPM, and key signature.\n  - Added instant Play circular buttons, quick-load chips for Deck A / Deck B, favorite toggles, and deletion affordances.\n  - Included a streamlined stream ingestion card with deck destination selection and progress indicators.\n\n- **Rock-Solid Playback Timeline & Scrubber**:\n  - Replaced the jittery slider with `DeckTimelineScrubber`, which separates user drag gestures from the engine\'s 60ms ticker updates.\n  - Seeking is debounced until release, preventing playback stutter, jumpy timestamps, or timeline displacement."
    modified_response: "All requested features, fixes, and design enhancements have been implemented and verified:\n\n- **Deck Mode Switching (1-Deck Default & 2-Decks Pro DJ Mode)**:\n  - Added a configuration toggle at the top of the Decks screen between **1 DECK (Solo)** and **2 DECKS (DJ)**, defaulting to 1-Deck mode.\n  - In **1-Deck Mode**, a dedicated solo audiophile console is presented featuring a large vinyl platter, expansive track metadata, audiophile spec tags (BPM, Key, Bit-Depth), smooth transport controls, and an interactive Channel A / Channel B selector.\n  - In **2-Decks Mode**, dual decks are displayed side-by-side with the center crossfader console, master rotary dial, and dual channel VU meters.\n\n- **Full Application Exit & Service Termination**:\n  - Added a dedicated **Power / Exit** action button in the top navigation bar.\n  - Tapping this opens a confirmation dialog that halts all deck playback, releases native `MediaPlayer` instances, stops the foreground `AuraPlaybackService`, clears notification controls, finishes active activities, and terminates the background process.\n\n- **Audio Playback & YouTube Sound Routing**:\n  - Resolved the YouTube silence issue by embedding the audio bridge WebViews directly into the active Compose hierarchy, forcing initialization unmuting and setting volume to 100% upon player readiness.\n  - Configured hardware audio session routing so audio plays through device speakers, headphones, or external DACs.\n\n- **Redesigned Library UI**:\n  - Fixed cramped track list items by transitioning to a clean 2-tier card layout. Song title and artist now receive full horizontal width with dedicated badges for source (**YouTube**, **Stream**, or **Local**), BPM, and key signature.\n  - Added instant Play circular buttons, quick-load chips for Deck A / Deck B, favorite toggles, and deletion affordances.\n  - Included a streamlined stream ingestion card with deck destination selection and progress indicators.\n\n- **Rock-Solid Playback Timeline & Scrubber**:\n  - Replaced the jittery slider with `DeckTimelineScrubber`, which separates user drag gestures from the engine\'s 60ms ticker updates.\n  - Seeking is debounced until release, preventing playback stutter, jumpy timestamps, or timeline displacement."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
